        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Get Over It, That '70s Show, But I'm a Cheerleader, Shrink, A Midsummer Night's Dream\n- People: Mila Kunis, Ben Foster, Kirsten Dunst, Melissa Sagemiller, Sisqó, Shane West, Colin Hanks, Zoe Saldana, Swoosie Kurtz, Ed Begley Jr., Carmen Electra, Martin Short, William Shakespeare\n- Companies: Ignite Entertainment\n- Topics: Film releases, Casting, Acting careers, Adaptations\n\nFacts:\n- Ignite Entertainment's films include But I'm a Cheerleader from 1999, Get Over It from 2001, and Shrink from 2009.\n- Get Over It is a 2001 American teen comedy film loosely based on William Shakespeare's A Midsummer Night's Dream.\n- Get Over It follows a high school senior who tries to win back his ex-girlfriend by joining the school play in which she and her new boyfriend are performing, despite his friends' advice.\n- Get Over It was released on March 9, 2001.\n- Get Over It stars Ben Foster, Kirsten Dunst, Melissa Sagemiller, Sisqó, Shane West, Colin Hanks, Zoe Saldana, Mila Kunis, Swoosie Kurtz, Ed Begley Jr., Carmen Electra, and Martin Short.\n- Mila Kunis, born August 14, 1983, is an American actress.\n- Before age 15, Mila Kunis appeared in several television series and commercials and gained her first significant role as Jackie Burkhart on That '70s Show.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
